          "path": "_m/g/c/p/u/royal-artillery-memorial-wp/royal-artillery-memorial-35810.jpg",
          "filename": "Royal Artillery Memorial (3581099408).jpg",
          "caption": "The Royal Artillery Memorial is a large stone memorial at Hyde Park Corner in London dedicated to casualties in the British Royal Regiment of Artillery in World War I.\nDesigned by Charles Sargeant Jagger (1885-1934) and dedicated in 1925, the memorial is in the form of a giant sculpture of a BL 9.2 inch Mk I howitzer upon a large plinth of Portland stone, with stone reliefs depicting the reality of war.\n\nThere are four bronze figures of artillery soldiers on the memorial as part of scenes reflecting the reality of war.",
          "alt": "The Royal Artillery Memorial is a large stone memorial at Hyde Park Corner in London dedicated to casualties in the British Royal Regiment of Artillery in World War I.\nDesigned by Charles Sargeant Jagger (1885-1934) and dedicated in 1925, the memorial is in the form of a giant sculpture of a BL 9.2 inch Mk I howitzer upon a large plinth of Portland stone, with stone reliefs depicting the reality of war.\n\nThere are four bronze figures of artillery soldiers on the memorial as part of scenes reflecting the reality of war.",
          "width": 1599,
          "height": 2132,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
          "artist": "Amanda Slater from Coventry, West Midlands, UK",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Royal_Artillery_Memorial_(3581099408).jpg",
